 },
 "notes": "Boxes are the PDF widgets (2 pages). The checkbox widgets are numbered 'Check Box1'..'Check Box114' (no 9); 17 is Hearing Loss/Problem, 69/70 are Drug Use Yes/No, 94 and 114 are the family and surgical NONE boxes. Personal history and surgical history boxes map to enum arrays with contains; single-choice groups (marital status, sexual activity, seatbelt, employment, exercise, abuse current/history) to enums with equals; tobacco types are multi-select (contains); Yes boxes and standalone items get bool_to_check, No boxes equals. Each family-history condition has a checkbox (bool_to_check on the relatives array: ticked when non-empty) and a relatives line (join). The medications answer spans three widgets; only line 1 carries the path. Pathless: Age (the schema keeps date_of_birth; age cannot be computed by a transform), medication lines 2-3, the 'None' line and None/Unknown/NONE boxes (an empty list, not expressible with contains), the social-history group header boxes (Alcohol Use, Employment, Marital Status, Sexual Activity, Seatbelt Use, Tobacco Use, Drug Use; their options carry the answer), 'I am a twin', and the biopsy results/date (not kept)."
}
